\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{A sector choice and its Gaussian data}
\date{2026-11-08}

\p{For the real [half-turn action](fdip-000L) on
#{H=\mathbb R^4}, the generator #{r\in C_2} acts by the
permutation #{(0\;2)(1\;3)}. Its group-algebra idempotent
#{e_+=(1+[r])/2} has image #{E_+} under the algebra action.
Taking the selected-background projector #{P=E_+} retains the
rank-2 space #{V_+} with the counting metric.
The scalar field is #{\mathbb R}; the group algebra and the
endomorphism algebra are associative unital
[algebras over that field](ca-0016). Their definition imposes
no commutativity requirement on multiplication.}

\p{For the alternating-cycle weights #{1,t,1,t} and #{m>0},
with #{t>0}, \ref{fdip-003S} supplies the commuting precision
and its positive block #{Q_+} in an orthonormal basis of #{V_+}.
In the [sufficient Gaussian data map](fdip-005E), #{j(b)} retains
this full precision along with #{P}; the selected-structure map
#{\sigma(b)} has precision #{Q_+} in that basis.
The representation and the choice of #{e_+} supply #{P}.
The raw selector map extracts that choice, while the retained
operator and law are derived from #{j(b)}.}

\p{The admissible comparisons are the directed or signed
[background arrows](fdip-005C), with their vertex counting
isometries #{U:H\to H'}. Their identities
#{Q'=UQU^{-1}} and #{P'=UPU^{-1}} give
##{\begin{aligned}
P'U&=U_XP,&U_X&=U|_X:X\to X',\\
C_{P'}&=U_XC_PU_X^{-1},&
S_{P'}&=U_XS_PU_X^{-1},\\
(U_X)_*\nu_b&=\nu_{b'}.
\end{aligned}}
Here the projection in the first line is viewed as #{P:H\to X}.
The representation is a supplier of the projector, not additional
data transported by these arrows. Comparing independently supplied
representations would require their intertwining as a further
condition. The squared-norm expectation from \ref{fdip-005K},
#{\mathbb E_{\nu_b}\|x\|^2=\trace_X C_P}
is invariant under this isometric transport; coordinate observables
use the pullback from #{X'} to #{X}.}

\p{Commutation with the symmetry is a constraint on the precision;
the positive weights and mass remain supplied choices; the retained
precision is derived. These mathematical roles leave their physical
provenance unspecified. The distinction among symmetry, bubble
initial conditions and local environment in the
[motivation](fdip-00AU) is a separate question: a freely supplied
coefficient has not thereby been assigned a cosmological origin,
and dependence on #{j(b)} supplies no physical environment map.
The idempotent selects a subspace without a dynamical rule for
choosing the representation or the sector.}
